    "created_at": "2017-09-14T08:48:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-14T08:48:40Z",
    "body": "I would enjoy getting rid of `<meta http-equiv='set-cookie' ...>` entirely. However, usage is [hovering around 0.02%](https://www.chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/1547), which is higher than I'd like to see. I get ~298 hits on that in HTTP Archive's 2017-07-15 run, with no real pattern to the few I spot-checked. *shrug*\r\n\r\nI think it's conceptually tied to `script-src`, since it seems to me that setting a cookie from a page _should_ require script access, but I'm not sure the impact is worth the churn. Perhaps @dveditz or @johnwilander has an opinion from Firefox/Safari respectively?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
